Thanks to those who mailed responses to my query on placing
an EXABYTE on Ethernet.  I received mail requesting
a general post of the ideas I have received.  A summary follows.

If the VAXstations are clustered with the computer having the
EXABYTE, you can run you backup job on that computer using LAVC
to access the disks of the VAXstations.

If the VAXstations are only DECnet nodes (our situation) then you
need VAX Distributed File Services.  This is a DEC product (DeskTop
VMS already has it but needs a licence, i.e., more money; hmmm they
get you either way!) which makes remote files look like local ones.

Trimarchi have "Etherboxes" for EXABYTE's, DAT's or optical disks
but there is no local distributor yet to demonstrate how they work.

