I guess it's not their emphasis.  The HSC50 has only 128K, the 40/70 512K,
and this has to be shared between 12->32 drives.  We're basically talking
obsolete technology - for the price you want something that commits about
256K->1M/drive for readahead and intelligent caching.  Unfortunatly, it
looks like rather than doing a good low end HSC, they're going to do
something increadibly expensive for the 9000 class machines.

> someone should make a BI board that provides raw disk registers to
