Hell, I wouldn't even mind if I could get a MSCP emulating SMD controller
for the BI bus.  This f**king SDI stuff is as bad as the Massbus for adding
cost w/o adding value.  It's is both slower and more expensive than directly
attaching the drives, not to mention you have to get derated Sabre drives
that are both slower and more expensive than the normal Sabre 1230's.

Somebody needs to take a hard look at the Megatape BI/SCSI controller
and see if it has any kind of diagnostic mode or other way to make it
more generally useful.

DEC's attempts to close off the BI bus have obviously bourne fruit, since
I can't get competitive peripherals either from DEC *or* third parties
and that wretched Sun 4 sits there running circles around my shiny new
DECsystem.  I don't want to think about new Sun "superservers" with IPI
drives and other fun stuff.

