It is my understanding that disconnecting is only necessary for devices which 
cannot fulfill the command in its entirety immediately, and therefore may 
(not must!) disconnect from the SCSI bus to be "nice".  If you will always 
have "enough" data to send, there is no reason to disconnect at all, and
therefore
you will only tie up the SCSI bus for as long as you are actually using
it.  The downside
is, if you must wait for any reason to complete the request, so will
every other
device on the SCSI bus, including the system disk.  So there might be a
performance
penalty.


